1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,536
For a child with mosaic variegated aneuploidy, a plausible medicine is only

2
00:00:05,536 --> 00:00:10,571
a starting point. We propose arimoclomol for laboratory testing, with explicit rules

3
00:00:10,571 --> 00:00:13,508
for deciding whether it deserves to advance.

4
00:00:13,508 --> 00:00:17,705
We have not demonstrated drug rescue or treated this child.

5
00:00:17,705 --> 00:00:22,740
Our contribution is a testable proposal, supported by working tools that others

6
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:23,580
can use.

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:31,438
The two identified variants affect the gene that makes Bub R one,

8
00:00:31,438 --> 00:00:34,107
a protein involved in chromosome separation.

9
00:00:34,107 --> 00:00:38,555
Their phase is inferred. The exact protein consequences remain unmeasured.

10
00:00:38,555 --> 00:00:43,892
The missense variant could reduce abundance, impair function, do both, or remain

11
00:00:43,892 --> 00:00:48,785
indeterminate. We compare full-length normal and altered protein at matched abundance.

12
00:00:48,785 --> 00:00:52,788
An isolated fragment's melting curve cannot settle that question.

13
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:59,252
Arimoclomol has a human approval in a different disease.

14
00:00:59,252 --> 00:01:03,643
Its reported effects depend on the cell and the stress.

15
00:01:03,643 --> 00:01:07,156
That makes exposure a gate, not a footnote.

16
00:01:07,156 --> 00:01:09,791
First, qualify the model and measurement.

17
00:01:09,791 --> 00:01:14,182
Second, test whether the proposed response occurs at relevant exposure.

18
00:01:14,182 --> 00:01:19,451
Third, require better chromosome segregation, while tracking division, survival and cell fate.

19
00:01:19,451 --> 00:01:22,086
More protein alone does not pass.

20
00:01:22,086 --> 00:01:27,355
Neither does an apparent improvement caused by stopping division or selectively losing

21
00:01:27,355 --> 00:01:32,625
abnormal cells. Failed controls are indeterminate; a valid drug negative stops that

22
00:01:32,625 --> 00:01:33,503
tested approach.

23
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:39,047
We also built a practical gene-to-condition navigator.

24
00:01:39,047 --> 00:01:44,213
Search a gene, inspect its candidate condition mappings, and follow the source

25
00:01:44,213 --> 00:01:49,380
evidence. It includes every row of a dated, two thousand and sixty-three

26
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:53,685
row register snapshot, including thirty-five unmapped rows and source disagreements.

27
00:01:53,685 --> 00:01:58,851
A match is not an eligibility decision, and no match is not

28
00:01:58,851 --> 00:02:02,295
evidence of ineligibility. Queries stay on the device.

29
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:09,644
Our interpretation canary checks that a model has actually answered.

30
00:02:09,644 --> 00:02:13,519
Real Splice A I inference passes six controls.

31
00:02:13,519 --> 00:02:19,332
A separate checker self-test rejects nine injected failures, including missing and nonfinite

32
00:02:19,332 --> 00:02:23,207
output. We distinguish those tests from clinical accuracy.

33
00:02:23,207 --> 00:02:29,019
A public-genome spike-in also demonstrates scale, while leaving diagnostic performance and knowledge

34
00:02:29,019 --> 00:02:29,988
leakage unresolved.

35
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:37,092
The next step is a laboratory test of full-length variant function and

36
00:02:37,092 --> 00:02:41,683
exposure-limited rescue. The proposal says what would advance the candidate and what

37
00:02:41,683 --> 00:02:46,275
would stop it. The reusable tools, source trail and plain-language explanation are

38
00:02:46,275 --> 00:02:49,336
delivered now. Clinical benefit remains to be earned.

39
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:53,163
That is the standard we want this work judged against.
